{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f003"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=post-consume-stale-deref; Search only snapshots/s01: audit for the lifetime/pointer-invalidation sibling of the seed revealed by fact f003 - parsers that cache a header or TLV pointer, then advance the buffer or cursor (skb_pull, ptr += n, length -= n) and afterwards re-dereference the stale pointer on error, break, reply-echo, or debug paths when the walk may have consumed all remaining bytes, reading past the end of the packet data. Model already reported, do not re-report it: the a2mp_chan_recv_cb error path re-reading hdr->code/hdr->ident from post-pull skb->data in net/bluetooth/a2mp.c:682-692. Enumerate OTHER instances across s01 net/ only: Bluetooth l2cap_core/hci_event/mgmt error replies echoing consumed command headers, netfilter/x_tables and conntrack helper error paths, qdisc processing of pulled header copies, cfg80211/mac80211 rx and mlme error paths, TCP/DCCP/SCTP/MPTCP option-parse error handling that touches a pointer after advancing it; classify each candidate safe/reported/unresolved with exact file:line source quotes, or give an evidence-backed negative result; save a structured artifact for s01 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f003"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=post-consume-stale-deref; Search only snapshots/s02: audit for the lifetime/pointer-invalidation sibling of the seed (mechanism established by fact f003's a2mp error-path finding; this mechanism lens has never been searched in this snapshot): code that caches a header/TLV pointer, advances the buffer or cursor (skb_pull, ptr += n, length -= n, skb->data moving forward), and then re-dereferences the stale pointer on error, break, reply-echo, or debug paths when consumption may have exhausted the data, reading past the end of the packet buffer. Enumerate across s02 net/ only: Bluetooth l2cap_core/hci_event/mgmt error replies that echo consumed command headers, netfilter/conntrack/synproxy helper error paths, qdisc paths including sch_cake ack-filter error handling over pulled stack copies, cfg80211/mac80211 rx and mlme error paths, TCP/DCCP/SCTP option-parse error handling touching a pointer after advance; classify each candidate with exact file:line source quotes or an evidence-backed negative result; save a structured artifact for s02 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f003"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=post-consume-stale-deref; Search only snapshots/s03: audit for the lifetime/pointer-invalidation sibling of the seed (mechanism established by fact f003's a2mp error-path finding; this mechanism lens has never been searched in this snapshot): parsers that cache a header/TLV pointer, advance the buffer or cursor (skb_pull, ptr += n, length -= n), and afterwards re-dereference the stale pointer on error, break, reply-echo, or debug paths when the walk may have consumed all bytes, reading packet-adjacent memory past the buffer end. Enumerate across s03 net/ only: Bluetooth (l2cap_core, hci_event/hci_sync, mgmt, iso) error replies echoing consumed headers, netfilter/conntrack/synproxy helper error paths, qdisc header processing, cfg80211/mac80211 rx/mlme error paths, TCP/MPTCP/SCTP option-parse error handling touching a pointer after advance; classify each candidate with exact file:line source quotes or an evidence-backed negative result; save a structured artifact for s03 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f006"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=len-arith-wrap; Search only snapshots/s01: audit for bounds enforcement defeated by unsigned arithmetic rather than a missing comparison (sibling mechanism surfaced by facts f006 and f011, distinct from the already-concluded optsize-body-clamp missing-clamp shape): remaining-length bookkeeping that subtracts a length differing from the true element advance so a size_t/u32 counter underflows toward (size_t)-1, and size derivations (size - hdr_len, dlen - 2, ALIGN(size,4) + hdrlen, len + overhead) that wrap 32-bit arithmetic so an existing remaining<2 / size<=remaining / off+len<=end check compares against a wrapped huge value, enabling OOB reads or memcpy/get_unaligned overruns of packet-derived buffers. Primary unresolved lead from f006: qrtr_endpoint_post in net/qrtr/qrtr.c (~lines 291/312/318, u32 size making ALIGN(size,4)+hdrlen wrap) - close it with concrete source evidence of reachable transports or reject it with evidence. Then enumerate sibling shapes across s01 net/ only (netlink/netfilter attribute size arithmetic, Bluetooth EIR/AMP length bookkeeping, wireless IE merge arithmetic, qdisc and protocol header size math); classify each candidate with exact file:line quotes or an evidence-backed negative; save a structured artifact for s01 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f006","f011"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=len-arith-wrap; Search only snapshots/s02: audit for unsigned-arithmetic corruption of length/size bookkeeping that makes an existing bounds check lie (mechanism revealed by facts f006 and f011; never searched in this snapshot): subtraction of a payload/field length that differs from the true element advance, underflowing a size_t/u32 remaining counter toward (size_t)-1; size derivations (size - hdr_len, dlen - 2, ALIGN(size,4) + hdrlen, len + overhead) that wrap 32-bit arithmetic so a subsequent remaining<2 / size<=remaining / off+len<=end comparison passes while the real buffer is smaller, driving OOB reads or memcpy overruns of packet-derived buffers. Enumerate across s02 net/ only: netlink attribute and netfilter/nftables size math, Bluetooth EIR/AD/A2MP length bookkeeping, cfg80211/mac80211 IE merge and element-length arithmetic including the scan.c MBSSID profile merge paths, qdisc and protocol header size computations, qrtr/rpmsg if present; classify each candidate with exact file:line source quotes or an evidence-backed negative result; save a structured artifact for s02 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["f001","f011"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=len-arith-wrap; Search only snapshots/s03: audit for unsigned-arithmetic corruption of length/size bookkeeping that defeats an existing bounds check (sibling mechanism of the seed revealed by facts f011 and f006; the eir_get_service_data eir_len -= dlen underflow to (size_t)-1 and the base_len = dlen - 2 underflow feeding memcpy at net/bluetooth/iso.c:2365 are already reported - find OTHER instances in this snapshot): subtraction of a length differing from the true element advance underflowing a remaining counter; size derivations (size - hdr_len, dlen - 2, ALIGN(size,4) + hdrlen, len + overhead) that wrap so remaining<2 / size<=remaining / off+len<=end checks pass while the true buffer is smaller; resulting OOB reads or memcpy/get_unaligned overruns of packet-derived buffers. Enumerate across s03 net/ only: Bluetooth EIR/AD/ISO/BIS length bookkeeping, cfg80211/mac80211 IE walk and merge arithmetic, netfilter/nftables size math, qrtr/rpmsg if present, protocol header and option size computations; classify each candidate with exact file:line quotes or an evidence-backed negative; save a structured artifact for s03 only."}
